WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Advertise your product or brand here
contact www.OpenSubtitles.org today

2
00:00:20.693 --> 00:00:23.863
There.

3
00:00:23.946 --> 00:00:25.322
It just hit.

4
00:00:27.282 --> 00:00:29.701
It's gotta be 40 stories. at least.

5
00:00:31.286 --> 00:00:32.847
Down!

6
00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:38.669
They're on all sides.
Half a dozen. at least.

7
00:00:38.753 --> 00:00:40.546
- I got a problem.
- Right with you.

8
00:00:40.629 --> 00:00:42.297
No. you don't get it. I can't
get a read on these guys.

9
00:00:42.381 --> 00:00:43.966
There's no sound. there's
no heartbeat. there's nothing.

10
00:00:44.049 --> 00:00:45.801
- They're trained to hide themselves.
- How do you know?

11
00:00:45.885 --> 00:00:47.887
Don't focus on the
fighters. track their weapons.

12
00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:49.971
- They have swords.
- They have swords. I can hear.

13
00:01:37.602 --> 00:01:38.770
Elektra. no!

14
00:01:54.036 --> 00:01:55.705
Matthew...

15
00:02:30.114 --> 00:02:31.448
So...

16
00:02:35.119 --> 00:02:37.747
who wants to get the hell out of here?

17
00:03:49.568 --> 00:03:51.027
She's losing too much blood.

18
00:03:51.111 --> 00:03:52.154
Hell of a scrape.

19
00:03:52.237 --> 00:03:53.613
Where are you taking her?

20
00:03:54.949 --> 00:03:56.951
They're still coming. Fast little shits.

21
00:03:58.285 --> 00:04:00.537
- Who are they. Stick?
- Bad time to chat.

22
00:04:33.528 --> 00:04:34.863
- Matty!
- On it!

23
00:04:39.118 --> 00:04:40.619
- Watch your ass.
- Yeah.

24
00:04:45.457 --> 00:04:47.459
No. no. no. No. she's dying.

25
00:04:47.542 --> 00:04:49.753
- Stick. she's dying.
-  Not if I can stop it.

26
00:04:49.836 --> 00:04:51.004
We need to get her to a hospital.

27
00:04:51.088 --> 00:04:53.674
Doctors can't help her. I can.

28
00:04:53.757 --> 00:04:55.759
We're going to your
place. It's her only shot.

29
00:04:55.842 --> 00:04:58.845
Sweetie. stay with me. Stay with me.

30
00:04:58.928 --> 00:05:00.472
Second wave. Brace her.

31
00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:17.239
End of that batch.

32
00:05:19.199 --> 00:05:20.659
There'll be more.

33
00:05:22.411 --> 00:05:24.038
Always more.

34
00:05:35.132 --> 00:05:38.177
I'm not gonna lie to you. This is bad.

35
00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:40.262
What's happening to her?

36
00:05:40.345 --> 00:05:42.014
You got baking soda?

37
00:05:42.097 --> 00:05:43.557
Yeah. in the fridge. why?

38
00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:46.893
To neutralize the
acid in the toilet bowl cleaner.

39
00:05:46.976 --> 00:05:49.646
Plus whiskey. pliers. black tea.

40
00:05:49.729 --> 00:05:51.773
Tell me what's going on. Stick.

41
00:05:51.856 --> 00:05:53.942
Do you wanna talk or
save your girlfriend?

42
00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.657
Her heart's skipping.

43
00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:03.076
Whiskey.

44
00:06:04.619 --> 00:06:07.831
The toxins in her
bloodstream are shutting everything down.

45
00:06:07.914 --> 00:06:08.957
Is she gonna live?

46
00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:10.416
Baking soda?

47
00:06:12.336 --> 00:06:13.837
I thought you got it.

48
00:06:17.466 --> 00:06:18.967
Matthew!

49
00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:21.511
I need pliers and hot tea.

50
00:06:24.598 --> 00:06:26.225
The pliers are behind you.

51
00:06:38.528 --> 00:06:40.822
Matthew...

52
00:06:40.905 --> 00:06:42.741
I'm here. I'm here.

53
00:06:44.534 --> 00:06:46.120
If I die...

54
00:06:46.203 --> 00:06:49.373
No. you're not gonna die. You hear me?

55
00:06:49.456 --> 00:06:51.166
Elektra. look at me.

56
00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:53.543
Hey. hey. focus on me.

57
00:06:53.627 --> 00:06:55.795
Breathe. Breathe.

58
00:06:55.879 --> 00:06:57.464
That's good. That's good.

59
00:06:57.547 --> 00:06:58.882
I'm sorry.

60
00:06:58.965 --> 00:07:01.218
I'm sorry I didn't tell you.

61
00:07:01.301 --> 00:07:02.469
Bring her in here!

62
00:07:02.552 --> 00:07:03.803
Yeah.

63
00:07:08.099 --> 00:07:09.351
One. two. three.

64
00:07:19.819 --> 00:07:21.280
- Clean sheets.
- Yeah.

65
00:07:26.118 --> 00:07:27.577
Can you save her?

66
00:07:27.661 --> 00:07:29.496
Not before I make her worse.

67
00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:32.582
Oh. Jesus! Stick. take it easy!

68
00:07:32.666 --> 00:07:34.668
Those blades were poisoned.

69
00:07:34.751 --> 00:07:36.211
She'll be dead in 20 minutes

70
00:07:36.295 --> 00:07:39.005
if I don't pull some
serious juju out of my ass.

71
00:07:39.088 --> 00:07:40.882
Make the goddamn tea!

72
00:07:44.428 --> 00:07:45.887
Easy.

73
00:07:57.482 --> 00:08:00.235
Easy. Easy. young lady. I'm right here.

74
00:08:08.618 --> 00:08:10.258
forgive those who trespass against us.

75
00:08:11.288 --> 00:08:14.082
Matty. use
that hearing of yours.

76
00:08:15.542 --> 00:08:16.876
How's her heart rate?

77
00:08:22.216 --> 00:08:24.426
Yeah. Yeah. it's good. It's steady.

78
00:08:26.553 --> 00:08:27.762
Sheets.

79
00:08:35.103 --> 00:08:36.855
Not too neat...

80
00:08:37.814 --> 00:08:39.941
but...

81
00:08:40.024 --> 00:08:41.735
it'll do.

82
00:08:41.818 --> 00:08:42.902
Tea?

83
00:08:48.617 --> 00:08:51.160
Thank you.

84
00:08:52.912 --> 00:08:54.206
Ah...

85
00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:27.614
She'll recover?

86
00:09:28.573 --> 00:09:30.158
Twenty-four hours will tell.

87
00:09:30.992 --> 00:09:33.077
I've known her to pull through worse.

88
00:09:35.372 --> 00:09:36.456
What'd you just say?

89
00:09:36.540 --> 00:09:39.709
Ellie's a real fighter. Always has been.

90
00:09:42.003 --> 00:09:43.547
You... You know her?

91
00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:45.211
I didn't mention that?

92
00:09:46.151 --> 00:09:48.677
What the hell's going
on? How do you know Elektra?

93
00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:50.762
- I'm not done in there.
- I want some answers!

94
00:09:50.845 --> 00:09:51.930
Everybody wants something.

95
00:09:52.013 --> 00:09:55.141
- Do you want me to throw you out?
- Not unless you want her to die.

96
00:10:02.607 --> 00:10:04.193
Sit down. Matty.

97
00:10:06.778 --> 00:10:07.946
Where is he?

98
00:10:08.822 --> 00:10:12.284
Um. I may have told him
just to stay home today.

99
00:10:12.367 --> 00:10:13.827
You what?

100
00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:15.620
He wasn't actually supposed to do it.

101
00:10:15.704 --> 00:10:18.457
Whoa. whoa. Foggy. what
the hell happened yesterday?

102
00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:19.874
I can't do this alone.

103
00:10:19.958 --> 00:10:21.585
I didn't even wanna take this case.

104
00:10:21.668 --> 00:10:24.754
- It'll be okay. I...
- The whole city is watching.

105
00:10:24.838 --> 00:10:26.130
If I screw up. I'd never work again.

106
00:10:26.214 --> 00:10:28.967
And. frankly. you'd probably never
work again. either. by association. which...

107
00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:31.845
Stop. Foggy. Stop thinking about
screwing up. about losing.

108
00:10:31.928 --> 00:10:33.304
You need to think about winning.

109
00:10:35.181 --> 00:10:38.017
Colonel Ray
Schoonover. United States Marine Corps.

110
00:10:38.101 --> 00:10:39.728
Do you swear to tell the truth.

111
00:10:39.811 --> 00:10:42.981
the whole truth and nothing but
the truth. so help you God?

112
00:10:43.523 --> 00:10:44.649
I do.

113
00:10:48.152 --> 00:10:49.988
You got this.

114
00:10:50.071 --> 00:10:51.656
Counsel?

115
00:10:59.623 --> 00:11:01.833
Colonel. how long have
you known the defendant?

116
00:11:01.916 --> 00:11:04.252
I'd say. the better part of a decade.

117
00:11:04.336 --> 00:11:06.004
Most of his career in the Marine Corps.

118
00:11:06.087 --> 00:11:08.882
So you're familiar with his
service in the Middle East?

119
00:11:08.965 --> 00:11:10.717
Afghanistan. Pakistan. Iran?

120
00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:12.844
Yes. very familiar.

121
00:11:12.927 --> 00:11:15.179
I wonder if you could tell us

122
00:11:15.263 --> 00:11:18.099
how Lieutenant Frank
Castle won the Navy Cross?

123
00:11:18.182 --> 00:11:21.520
Due to the nature of that
mission. you'll have to understand that

124
00:11:21.603 --> 00:11:23.772
the precise circumstances
are classified.

125
00:11:27.567 --> 00:11:28.777
Um...

126
00:11:30.487 --> 00:11:32.989
How about the part that's not?

127
00:11:33.865 --> 00:11:36.325
Lieutenant Frank Castle
was part of a small team.

128
00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:38.495
He was conducting a close
target reconnaissance

129
00:11:38.578 --> 00:11:40.622
in the vicinity of the Hindu Kush.

130
00:11:40.705 --> 00:11:44.876
The mission became compromised. taking
enemy contact on three sides.

131
00:11:46.836 --> 00:11:49.255
Lieutenant Castle wanted to abort.

132
00:11:49.338 --> 00:11:53.259
Said the mission was a bust. pulling
the plug would save lives.

133
00:11:53.342 --> 00:11:56.179
- Officer in charge said "no."
-  And why was that?

134
00:11:56.262 --> 00:11:58.382
Maybe he
wanted more medals on his chest.

135
00:11:58.432 --> 00:12:00.600
Doesn't matter. Either
way. Frank was right.

136
00:12:00.684 --> 00:12:04.062
They were cut off. boxed into a canyon.

137
00:12:04.145 --> 00:12:06.105
And what happened next?

138
00:12:06.189 --> 00:12:08.983
Within the first hour. the
officer in charge of that mission

139
00:12:09.067 --> 00:12:11.027
got his arm blown off.

140
00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:13.362
So Lieutenant Castle assumed command.

141
00:12:13.447 --> 00:12:16.491
His only goal was to
get his men out alive.

142
00:12:16.575 --> 00:12:19.703
The enemy had set up an ambush

143
00:12:19.786 --> 00:12:23.122
at the only LZ that would
accommodate one of our birds.

144
00:12:23.206 --> 00:12:24.207
Sorry. Colonel?

145
00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:28.628
LZ is a landing zone that
can accommodate a helicopter.

146
00:12:28.712 --> 00:12:32.466
So the enemy. they
block this landing zone.

147
00:12:32.549 --> 00:12:35.969
knowing it was the only shot
the team had to get out alive.

148
00:12:36.052 --> 00:12:37.887
All they had to do was wait.

149
00:12:37.971 --> 00:12:40.098
They knew that Frank's
team had to come to them.

150
00:12:40.181 --> 00:12:41.224
Fish in a barrel.

151
00:12:41.307 --> 00:12:42.559
So to speak.

152
00:12:42.642 --> 00:12:44.603
Only fish don't know they're gonna die.

153
00:12:44.686 --> 00:12:47.063
These men did.

154
00:12:47.146 --> 00:12:52.819
Frank went to the LZ all by
himself to draw the bastards away.

155
00:12:52.902 --> 00:12:54.943
Why didn't he
order one of his men to do it?

156
00:12:54.946 --> 00:12:55.947
He certainly could have.

157
00:12:56.781 --> 00:12:57.949
Not his style.

158
00:13:00.326 --> 00:13:03.955
So the men hear the fire fight
break out. All hell breaks loose.

159
00:13:04.038 --> 00:13:06.040
Frank against God knows how many.

160
00:13:06.124 --> 00:13:08.292
And then there was silence.

161
00:13:08.376 --> 00:13:12.672
The team thinks. "That's it.
Frank's dead. and we're next."

162
00:13:14.758 --> 00:13:18.052
Next sound they hear is
the helos. the helicopters.

163
00:13:18.136 --> 00:13:20.972
They get to the landing
zone. you know what they see?

164
00:13:22.098 --> 00:13:24.559
Frank Castle. standing there. grinning.

165
00:13:24.643 --> 00:13:28.271
Thirty-two muj surrounding him. all dead.

166
00:13:28.354 --> 00:13:31.816
Son of a gun cleared that
entire LZ all by himself.

167
00:13:32.526 --> 00:13:33.652
How?

168
00:13:34.443 --> 00:13:36.655
By being Frank Castle.

169
00:13:36.738 --> 00:13:38.657
- And his men survived?
- All of 'em.

170
00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:41.618
Including the idiot officer that
got 'em trapped in the first place.

171
00:13:41.701 --> 00:13:44.871
If you had to sum up Frank
Castle. how would you do it?

172
00:13:44.954 --> 00:13:46.873
I would say Frank Castle is a man

173
00:13:46.956 --> 00:13:50.209
who would gladly give his
life to keep others safe.

174
00:13:50.293 --> 00:13:52.420
And the
crimes he's accused of today?

175
00:13:52.503 --> 00:13:54.297
Could the man you
knew have committed them?

176
00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:55.924
Absolutely not.

177
00:13:57.216 --> 00:14:00.887
Lieutenant Frank
Castle that I know is a hero.

178
00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:02.806
A man who deserves our respect...

179
00:14:03.890 --> 00:14:05.349
and our gratitude.

180
00:14:07.101 --> 00:14:08.311
Not the same man.

181
00:14:09.228 --> 00:14:11.815
Thank you. sir. No more
questions. Your Honor.

182
00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.193
People?

183
00:14:23.326 --> 00:14:27.413
I'd like to personally thank you for
your service to this country. Colonel.

184
00:14:27.496 --> 00:14:29.916
My father served in Vietnam.

185
00:14:29.999 --> 00:14:32.794
- Do you know what he told me about medals?
- No. ma'am.

186
00:14:32.877 --> 00:14:35.880
He said the only people who
truly know what happened

187
00:14:35.964 --> 00:14:37.256
are the ones that were there.

188
00:14:38.507 --> 00:14:40.176
You told a nice story. Colonel...

189
00:14:40.719 --> 00:14:44.806
but how can we know that it
happened the way you described?

190
00:14:44.889 --> 00:14:48.434
Well. perhaps I wasn't
clear. I was there. ma'am.

191
00:14:49.518 --> 00:14:52.814
That officer that didn't listen
to Frank. got his men trapped...

192
00:14:53.397 --> 00:14:54.475
you're looking at him.

193
00:14:54.566 --> 00:14:56.068
And believe me when I tell you.

194
00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:59.570
I thank God every day that
I only lost my arm.

195
00:15:00.154 --> 00:15:03.700
That man saved my life. the
lives of his entire team.

196
00:15:04.868 --> 00:15:06.202
If it was up to me.

197
00:15:06.285 --> 00:15:08.913
he'd have a Medal of
Honor hanging around his neck.

198
00:15:11.124 --> 00:15:13.918
No further questions at
this time. Your Honor.

199
00:15:16.588 --> 00:15:18.006
How'd you miss that in his file?

200
00:15:18.089 --> 00:15:19.423
All the names were redacted.

201
00:15:19.507 --> 00:15:20.549
Not good.

202
00:15:20.634 --> 00:15:22.051
No shit.

203
00:15:22.135 --> 00:15:24.721
Hey. Matt couldn't have done it better.

204
00:15:25.513 --> 00:15:26.640
It was good.

205
00:15:35.231 --> 00:15:36.482
How is she?

206
00:15:36.565 --> 00:15:39.568
Well... she'll live.

207
00:15:40.695 --> 00:15:42.030
Yeah? You sure?

208
00:15:42.113 --> 00:15:43.782
Sure as I am of anything.

209
00:15:49.871 --> 00:15:51.915
Jesus. didn't we do this already?

210
00:15:51.998 --> 00:15:53.291
Start talking. Stick.

211
00:15:53.374 --> 00:15:55.251
It's about the war.

212
00:15:55.334 --> 00:15:56.961
What is?

213
00:15:57.045 --> 00:15:58.337
All of it.

214
00:15:58.963 --> 00:16:02.383
Roxxon. Midland
Circle. the damn hole. Elektra...

215
00:16:02.466 --> 00:16:05.428
All right. you've been using this
war as an excuse since the day I met you.

216
00:16:05.511 --> 00:16:08.014
and you still haven't told
me a goddamn thing about it.

217
00:16:08.097 --> 00:16:09.683
- You know what I think?
- Tell me.

218
00:16:09.766 --> 00:16:11.517
I think you're full of shit.

219
00:16:11.600 --> 00:16:13.186
I don't think there is any war.

220
00:16:14.187 --> 00:16:16.605
I think you're just a sick old
fighter dying to hit people.

221
00:16:16.690 --> 00:16:19.123
so you make up stories to
justify your behavior.

222
00:16:20.694 --> 00:16:23.238
And then. you rope in the wounded...

223
00:16:23.321 --> 00:16:26.282
so that you can sit back and
watch them throw away their lives.

224
00:16:26.365 --> 00:16:27.742
and you can feel important.

225
00:16:27.826 --> 00:16:28.993
Sit down.

226
00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:33.206
Sit down. Matty.

227
00:16:39.503 --> 00:16:41.756
It all began centuries ago.

228
00:16:41.840 --> 00:16:43.341
Nobody knows how many.

229
00:16:43.424 --> 00:16:45.176
but the shit we're dipping into...

230
00:16:45.802 --> 00:16:47.470
is ancient.

231
00:16:48.054 --> 00:16:53.601
Back then. warlords and their
gangs ruled the countryside.

232
00:16:53.685 --> 00:16:56.020
Not that much different from today.

233
00:16:56.938 --> 00:17:02.819
Bloodthirsty. greedy brutes after
loot. pussy. booze. same ol'. same ol'.

234
00:17:03.987 --> 00:17:06.239
But... one day.

235
00:17:06.322 --> 00:17:09.408
one of these collections of assholes

236
00:17:09.492 --> 00:17:13.287
comes across a thing they
can barely understand.

237
00:17:14.205 --> 00:17:15.539
Real treasure.

238
00:17:15.623 --> 00:17:18.292
Not gold. or rubies. or any of that.

239
00:17:21.254 --> 00:17:23.131
They found the secret.

240
00:17:24.048 --> 00:17:25.466
What secret?

241
00:17:25.549 --> 00:17:26.843
Immortality.

242
00:17:27.761 --> 00:17:30.054
Bringing the dead back to life.

243
00:17:30.638 --> 00:17:32.306
Come on. Stick.

244
00:17:33.516 --> 00:17:36.477
I thought you
were a Catholic. Matty.

245
00:17:37.645 --> 00:17:42.108
Doesn't your whole belief system
hinge on one guy pulling that off?

246
00:17:45.987 --> 00:17:47.196
So...

247
00:17:48.907 --> 00:17:51.325
Free from the fear of death.

248
00:17:51.409 --> 00:17:56.915
these pieces of shit step
up. kill their master. take over.

249
00:17:56.998 --> 00:17:59.083
and paint the shores of the Far East

250
00:17:59.167 --> 00:18:02.170
with the blood of
anybody who stands in their way.

251
00:18:03.797 --> 00:18:07.926
They grow in size. power. wealth...

252
00:18:09.385 --> 00:18:11.512
spread across Asia...

253
00:18:11.595 --> 00:18:14.182
and finally give themselves a name.

254
00:18:15.183 --> 00:18:16.559
Yaminote.

255
00:18:17.894 --> 00:18:19.687
It means. "The Hand."

256
00:18:21.564 --> 00:18:23.566
And did they have a goal?

257
00:18:23.649 --> 00:18:27.195
Weapons. It's always weapons.

258
00:18:27.278 --> 00:18:29.613
Like. guns. bombs?

259
00:18:29.697 --> 00:18:30.865
Worse.

260
00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:33.993
Thing called a Black Sky.

261
00:18:34.452 --> 00:18:37.413
So. what's it do. this. uh. Black Sky?

262
00:18:37.496 --> 00:18:39.290
Nobody knows exactly.

263
00:18:41.667 --> 00:18:42.751
Why not?

264
00:18:42.836 --> 00:18:45.797
Because they've never activated one.

265
00:18:46.923 --> 00:18:49.550
They've tried. They'll try again.

266
00:18:51.177 --> 00:18:52.345
But...

267
00:18:54.347 --> 00:18:56.557
the Hand made one mistake.

268
00:18:57.141 --> 00:18:58.351
They made enemies.

269
00:18:58.434 --> 00:18:59.602
Bingo.

270
00:19:01.562 --> 00:19:03.647
Some say it was just a kid.

271
00:19:04.899 --> 00:19:09.487
Hand comes into his
village. kills everyone...

272
00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:11.239
almost.

273
00:19:11.780 --> 00:19:17.661
Kid... pulls the knife from
the breast of his dead mother...

274
00:19:17.745 --> 00:19:20.414
and goes to work.

275
00:19:22.125 --> 00:19:25.211
He cuts down some of the
Hand's finest warriors.

276
00:19:26.963 --> 00:19:30.758
They're lying dead... kid's standing.

277
00:19:32.051 --> 00:19:35.679
They give him a name. The Chaste.

278
00:19:36.264 --> 00:19:38.432
And he's just one kid? Alone?

279
00:19:38.516 --> 00:19:42.395
Kid grows up. rounds
up every warrior he can.

280
00:19:43.396 --> 00:19:47.608
Men. women. young. old. doesn't
matter as long as they kick ass.

281
00:19:47.691 --> 00:19:49.110
And they do.

282
00:19:49.193 --> 00:19:51.404
Without mercy.

283
00:19:54.532 --> 00:19:58.369
And the only protection this
world has against the Hand.

284
00:20:01.247 --> 00:20:02.331
Wow.

285
00:20:04.333 --> 00:20:07.128
Now. in this fairy tale...

286
00:20:08.546 --> 00:20:11.340
you're the Chaste. right? That's...

287
00:20:11.424 --> 00:20:13.051
Is that it?

288
00:20:15.469 --> 00:20:17.263
It's why I didn't tell you.

289
00:20:17.346 --> 00:20:20.058
No. no. it's... It's good. It
leaves you front and center.

290
00:20:20.558 --> 00:20:23.561
Finding the Hand. keeping
the Black Skies at bay.

291
00:20:23.644 --> 00:20:25.729
Murdering when it suits you.

292
00:20:27.065 --> 00:20:28.691
Believe it or don't.

293
00:20:29.692 --> 00:20:33.947
The fact remains that the
city you're sworn to protect

294
00:20:34.030 --> 00:20:37.658
is ground zero in a war it
doesn't even know is happening.

295
00:20:37.741 --> 00:20:39.868
That hole is just the start.

296
00:20:41.704 --> 00:20:44.623
So. you can kill. die.

297
00:20:44.707 --> 00:20:49.003
or sit on your ass and
watch Hell's Kitchen burn...

298
00:20:50.671 --> 00:20:56.177
but this war is bigger than
you. or me. or any of our...

299
00:20:58.762 --> 00:21:00.264
problems.

300
00:21:00.348 --> 00:21:03.935
And you've pulled Elektra
to your side. haven't you?

301
00:21:04.018 --> 00:21:06.062
Welcome to the world. kid.

302
00:21:09.607 --> 00:21:12.783
Elektra works for me.

303
00:21:20.330 --> 00:21:22.370
The bullet
penetrated Mr. Castle's skull

304
00:21:22.453 --> 00:21:23.621
in the lower right quadrant.

305
00:21:23.704 --> 00:21:26.624
or more specifically. the
sphenofrontal suture.

306
00:21:26.707 --> 00:21:30.253
which is the cranial suture between
the sphenoid bone and the frontal bones.

307
00:21:30.336 --> 00:21:31.587
both here and here.

308
00:21:33.256 --> 00:21:35.841
I believe what my expert
witness is trying to convey

309
00:21:35.924 --> 00:21:38.761
is that my client.
Frank Castle. was shot...

310
00:21:38.844 --> 00:21:41.930
point blank. execution
style. in the head.

311
00:21:43.224 --> 00:21:47.937
Could you please describe the damage
Mr. Castle sustained from the bullet?

312
00:21:48.021 --> 00:21:49.981
It fragmented
on impact. causing damage

313
00:21:50.064 --> 00:21:52.941
in both the right frontal lobe
and temporal lobe of his brain.

314
00:21:53.026 --> 00:21:55.403
What are the effects of such an injury?

315
00:21:55.486 --> 00:21:58.947
Mr. Castle is suffering
from what we call sympathetic storming.

316
00:21:59.032 --> 00:22:01.534
It's a heightened and
ongoing state of fight or flight.

317
00:22:01.617 --> 00:22:04.828
in which the sympathetic
nervous system is hyperactive.

318
00:22:04.912 --> 00:22:08.624
As if he is reliving the
incident of trauma over and over again.

319
00:22:09.250 --> 00:22:12.128
It can plunge a seemingly
peaceful individual into...

320
00:22:12.211 --> 00:22:14.297
mental and emotional chaos.

321
00:22:14.380 --> 00:22:16.757
It sure sounds a lot like PTSD.

322
00:22:16.840 --> 00:22:18.384
No. that's not where we're going.

323
00:22:18.467 --> 00:22:19.968
Just... listen.

324
00:22:20.053 --> 00:22:21.929
Could you define it
for the jury. please?

325
00:22:22.013 --> 00:22:24.265
Extreme emotional disturbance.

326
00:22:24.348 --> 00:22:25.933
It's twofold.

327
00:22:26.016 --> 00:22:29.353
First. the defendant is so
emotionally disturbed that he loses control.

328
00:22:29.437 --> 00:22:32.606
And second. the defendant has
a reasonable explanation

329
00:22:32.690 --> 00:22:34.692
for said disturbance.
from his point of view.

330
00:22:34.775 --> 00:22:38.737
Are you aware that Frank
Castle's wife. son. and daughter

331
00:22:38.821 --> 00:22:40.739
were all murdered right in front of him

332
00:22:40.823 --> 00:22:42.908
when he sustained the
brain injury in question?

333
00:22:42.991 --> 00:22:44.368
An injury which. you say.

334
00:22:44.452 --> 00:22:48.081
keeps him in a perpetual
state of mental and emotional chaos?

335
00:22:48.164 --> 00:22:49.165
I am. yes.

336
00:22:49.248 --> 00:22:52.293
With that in mind. would you say
that Frank Castle's mental state

337
00:22:52.376 --> 00:22:56.714
satisfies the definition of "extreme
emotional disturbance"?

338
00:22:56.797 --> 00:22:58.966
Objection.
calls for a conclusion.

339
00:22:59.049 --> 00:23:01.469
Your Honor. Dr. Lee
is an expert on the brain.

340
00:23:01.552 --> 00:23:03.512
He is qualified to an opinion.

341
00:23:03.596 --> 00:23:07.683
and said opinion is not only
relevant. but imperative to the case.

342
00:23:09.685 --> 00:23:11.354
Overruled.

343
00:23:11.437 --> 00:23:12.563
Dr. Lee?

344
00:23:12.646 --> 00:23:15.983
Personally. I do
believe he is suffering from EED. yes.

345
00:23:16.066 --> 00:23:19.695
And one who's suffering from
extreme emotional disturbance.

346
00:23:19.778 --> 00:23:23.824
is it possible to
willfully premeditate a crime?

347
00:23:23.907 --> 00:23:26.660
Any infractions would be
considered crimes of passion.

348
00:23:27.745 --> 00:23:29.497
How many of your other patients

349
00:23:29.580 --> 00:23:33.000
witnessed their families being brutally
murdered right in front of them?

350
00:23:33.083 --> 00:23:34.918
Other than Frank Castle?

351
00:23:35.002 --> 00:23:36.254
He's the only one.

352
00:23:36.337 --> 00:23:39.840
And so would you say the
circumstances surrounding Frank's mental state

353
00:23:39.923 --> 00:23:42.468
is different than
those of your other patients?

354
00:23:42.551 --> 00:23:43.802
I would.

355
00:23:44.803 --> 00:23:48.391
And what exactly would that
difference be. in simple terms?

356
00:23:48.474 --> 00:23:50.559
Frank Castle's been through hell.

357
00:23:51.477 --> 00:23:52.603
Thank you.

358
00:23:52.686 --> 00:23:54.146
You killed my dad!

359
00:23:54.230 --> 00:23:55.689
I don't give a shit what
you've been through!

360
00:23:55.773 --> 00:23:57.525
- Order! Order in the court!
-  You killed him!

361
00:23:57.608 --> 00:24:00.236
- I saw him in his coffin...
- Please remove that young man now.

362
00:24:00.319 --> 00:24:02.571
He was my
dad. and now he's gone!

363
00:24:03.989 --> 00:24:08.035
I'm now instructing each and every one
of you to disregard that outburst

364
00:24:08.118 --> 00:24:11.580
and to not let it
influence your opinions on this case.

365
00:24:13.957 --> 00:24:15.334
I did that.

366
00:24:16.544 --> 00:24:17.545
Right?

367
00:24:19.547 --> 00:24:22.300
That kid. I took his
father from him. I did that.

368
00:24:23.801 --> 00:24:25.719
- Yeah. you did.
- Uh-huh.

369
00:24:28.847 --> 00:24:31.350
Look. Frank. I can't judge you.

370
00:24:35.854 --> 00:24:38.524
That was tough in
there for you. right? It was...

371
00:24:38.607 --> 00:24:40.234
It was. um. hard?

372
00:24:44.071 --> 00:24:45.448
Yeah.

373
00:24:48.242 --> 00:24:49.868
Okay.

374
00:24:49.952 --> 00:24:52.371
You gotta do something for me.

375
00:24:52.455 --> 00:24:54.122
Hmm?

376
00:24:54.207 --> 00:24:56.250
I need you to take the stand.

377
00:24:56.334 --> 00:24:57.751
Come on. for what? Why would I...

378
00:24:57.835 --> 00:25:01.255
The jury has to know what happened to
you. what you go through every single day.

379
00:25:01.339 --> 00:25:03.841
After this afternoon...

380
00:25:03.924 --> 00:25:06.344
I don't think we have any other shot.

381
00:25:06.427 --> 00:25:07.523
What?

382
00:25:07.669 --> 00:25:09.869
And what do you
think is gonna happen here?

383
00:25:09.930 --> 00:25:10.931
We're not gonna win this thing.

384
00:25:11.014 --> 00:25:12.975
No. but we can still reduce the charges.

385
00:25:14.184 --> 00:25:17.730
Look. that might not be important
to you. but it is important to me.

386
00:25:18.356 --> 00:25:21.275
All of them. they all
think that you're a monster.

387
00:25:21.359 --> 00:25:23.444
But I know that you're not. You're not!

388
00:25:26.113 --> 00:25:28.073
You sure about that?

389
00:25:29.492 --> 00:25:31.827
What if I find these men that
did that to my family?

390
00:25:31.910 --> 00:25:32.911
What if...

391
00:25:35.248 --> 00:25:37.207
What if nothing changes?

392
00:25:40.127 --> 00:25:42.255
What if this is just me now?

393
00:25:47.593 --> 00:25:49.928
Then don't you deserve
to know that. too?

394
00:25:56.477 --> 00:25:57.811
Foggy!

395
00:25:57.895 --> 00:25:58.979
Hey.

396
00:26:00.356 --> 00:26:03.108
He'll do it. He'll take the stand.

397
00:26:03.191 --> 00:26:04.943
- Are you serious?
- Yeah.

398
00:26:05.027 --> 00:26:07.655
Look. unless you have
a better idea. I think...

399
00:26:07.738 --> 00:26:09.657
How did we even get here?

400
00:26:09.740 --> 00:26:11.492
This guy's a murderer.

401
00:26:11.575 --> 00:26:14.453
He's killed fathers and
brothers. You heard that kid.

402
00:26:14.537 --> 00:26:15.996
Why are we helping him?

403
00:26:18.999 --> 00:26:22.711
Do you think that Frank is
completely and totally mentally healthy?

404
00:26:23.379 --> 00:26:25.172
- I think he's batshit.
- Yeah?

405
00:26:25.255 --> 00:26:27.341
Well. then that's why you help him.

406
00:26:28.133 --> 00:26:30.386
Put him on the stand. Foggy.

407
00:26:30.469 --> 00:26:32.054
Shit. Okay.

408
00:26:32.846 --> 00:26:34.723
- One caveat. though.
- Okay.

409
00:26:34.807 --> 00:26:37.059
- We get Matt to do the questioning.
- No.

410
00:26:37.142 --> 00:26:38.894
- Yes.
-  No.

411
00:26:38.977 --> 00:26:41.939
You're doing great. okay? You're
making Reyes play defense.

412
00:26:42.022 --> 00:26:43.573
You... you don't need Matt for this.

413
00:26:43.574 --> 00:26:44.900
- I do. Karen!
- Why do you always do this?

414
00:26:44.983 --> 00:26:47.653
Why do you put Matt in the driver's
seat when you can do this yourself?

415
00:26:47.736 --> 00:26:49.488
Matt and I are partners for a reason.

416
00:26:49.572 --> 00:26:51.178
There's some things that I'm better at.

417
00:26:51.202 --> 00:26:52.807
and there's things that he's better at.

418
00:26:52.866 --> 00:26:54.284
This is something that
he'll be better at.

419
00:26:54.368 --> 00:26:55.870
He's barely spent two
seconds with Frank.

420
00:26:55.953 --> 00:26:58.664
I know. but that kid nearly
destroyed us in there.

421
00:26:58.747 --> 00:27:02.167
And at this moment. Matt is the
right person to question Frank.

422
00:27:02.250 --> 00:27:03.627
He just is.

423
00:27:05.754 --> 00:27:07.423
Okay.

424
00:27:07.506 --> 00:27:08.507
I'll get him.

425
00:27:31.196 --> 00:27:33.491
- I'm sorry...
- When we met...

426
00:27:35.951 --> 00:27:37.370
was it fate?

427
00:27:39.037 --> 00:27:40.038
Was it luck?

428
00:27:42.541 --> 00:27:44.251
Or was I a mission?

429
00:27:50.424 --> 00:27:52.050
Mission.

430
00:28:11.487 --> 00:28:15.449
Stick trained me a long
time. like he trained you.

431
00:28:15.991 --> 00:28:18.786
He's not a sentimental
man. but he wanted you back.

432
00:28:21.622 --> 00:28:24.958
He wanted you to forget
about law. your friends...

433
00:28:25.918 --> 00:28:26.919
your city.

434
00:28:28.462 --> 00:28:30.423
He thought I could distract you.

435
00:28:32.090 --> 00:28:33.801
He was right.

436
00:28:33.884 --> 00:28:34.927
No.

437
00:28:36.261 --> 00:28:39.306
Because I did the thing I
promised him I'd never do.

438
00:28:40.474 --> 00:28:42.768
I fell in love with you. Matthew.

439
00:28:43.811 --> 00:28:46.188
Listen to my heartbeat. if you must.

440
00:28:46.271 --> 00:28:48.106
You know it's true.

441
00:28:50.776 --> 00:28:54.613
Stick told me about some secret
Japanese organization.

442
00:28:55.614 --> 00:28:56.824
The Hand.

443
00:28:56.907 --> 00:28:59.868
They won't stop until they've
infiltrated your whole city.

444
00:28:59.952 --> 00:29:02.996
Killed every last member of the Chaste.

445
00:29:03.080 --> 00:29:05.123
- Stick...
- You.

446
00:29:05.207 --> 00:29:07.292
We
live on the front lines.

447
00:29:07.835 --> 00:29:09.628
Like it or not.

448
00:29:09.712 --> 00:29:11.755
It doesn't mean we have
to fight Stick's way.

449
00:29:11.839 --> 00:29:14.717
He kills his
enemies. and we don't have to.

450
00:29:14.800 --> 00:29:16.802
You make that
choice sound so easy.

451
00:29:16.885 --> 00:29:19.680
No. it's not
easy. It's impossible.

452
00:29:20.305 --> 00:29:24.560
But it's a choice and it's a
choice that I remake every single day.

453
00:29:24.643 --> 00:29:27.187
Every second. sometimes.

454
00:29:27.270 --> 00:29:29.106
And you can. too.

455
00:29:29.189 --> 00:29:31.524
Matthew. there are things
about me you don't know.

456
00:29:31.609 --> 00:29:32.901
- I don't need to know.
- I want you to.

457
00:29:32.985 --> 00:29:35.195
I don't care. whatever
you've done in the past...

458
00:29:35.278 --> 00:29:37.865
Elektra. whoever you've chosen
to be. you're free now. all right?

459
00:29:37.948 --> 00:29:40.117
You could have killed those
men at the hole. but you didn't.

460
00:29:40.200 --> 00:29:41.452
Because you're not Stick.

461
00:29:41.535 --> 00:29:44.955
And screw him for ever making you feel
like you might be. even for a second.

462
00:29:45.038 --> 00:29:46.414
- He can hear you.
- I don't care.

463
00:29:46.499 --> 00:29:49.126
When you were hurt. when I
thought I might lose you. I...

464
00:29:50.878 --> 00:29:52.463
I...

465
00:29:52.546 --> 00:29:54.507
I felt hollow.

466
00:29:55.799 --> 00:29:57.718
Now. I have no reason to trust you.

467
00:29:57.801 --> 00:30:00.428
You've lied to me more
times than I can count.

468
00:30:00.513 --> 00:30:02.515
But if you leave Stick...

469
00:30:04.266 --> 00:30:05.476
be with me.

470
00:30:06.644 --> 00:30:08.812
Fight this war by my side.

471
00:30:08.896 --> 00:30:10.105
My way.

472
00:30:12.315 --> 00:30:13.567
Our way.

473
00:30:15.360 --> 00:30:17.404
Why are you so good?

474
00:30:21.617 --> 00:30:22.868
I'm not.

475
00:30:24.495 --> 00:30:26.038
Yes.

476
00:30:28.415 --> 00:30:30.501
There's a light inside you.

477
00:30:34.171 --> 00:30:36.674
I tried to snuff it out in college.

478
00:30:38.967 --> 00:30:40.803
I'm so lucky I failed.

479
00:30:47.392 --> 00:30:48.686
Someone... someone's here.

480
00:30:49.728 --> 00:30:51.313
You got company.

481
00:30:52.773 --> 00:30:54.024
Hey.

482
00:30:56.735 --> 00:30:57.903
Karen...

483
00:30:58.862 --> 00:31:00.363
Hi.

484
00:31:00.864 --> 00:31:03.576
Um. let's. uh...

485
00:31:03.659 --> 00:31:04.910
- let's go somewhere.
- No. Why?

486
00:31:04.993 --> 00:31:06.579
- So we can talk.
- I don't want to.

487
00:31:06.662 --> 00:31:08.247
I know this looks
crazy. but it's really not.

488
00:31:08.330 --> 00:31:10.165
It
doesn't... It doesn't matter.

489
00:31:10.916 --> 00:31:13.794
Frank Castle's going to
take the stand tomorrow.

490
00:31:13.877 --> 00:31:15.671
And your friend could use your help.

491
00:31:16.672 --> 00:31:17.756
That's all.

492
00:31:20.008 --> 00:31:21.594
Nice meetin' ya.

493
00:31:33.063 --> 00:31:35.190
Fan club's here.

494
00:31:35.273 --> 00:31:38.276
Word must have gotten
out about Frank testifying.

495
00:31:38.360 --> 00:31:40.696
Matt better show.

496
00:31:41.780 --> 00:31:44.199
If he doesn't. we'll survive. Right?

497
00:31:59.632 --> 00:32:01.008
Karen. I'm so sorry about...

498
00:32:01.091 --> 00:32:03.636
Uh. Foggy wants to walk
through some things with you.

499
00:32:10.100 --> 00:32:11.852
Yeah. you wanted me here?

500
00:32:11.935 --> 00:32:12.978
Wow.

501
00:32:13.061 --> 00:32:14.354
Let's be clear.

502
00:32:16.064 --> 00:32:18.734
You're not here because you're
a better lawyer or person.

503
00:32:18.817 --> 00:32:22.362
You're here because you're almost as
crazy as Frank Castle. and that's it.

504
00:32:22.445 --> 00:32:24.281
So you called me here to insult me?

505
00:32:24.364 --> 00:32:27.159
I called you here to
be useful. for a change.

506
00:32:27.242 --> 00:32:29.745
We need to get Frank to tell
his story in a way that keeps him

507
00:32:29.828 --> 00:32:31.872
out of prison and alive.

508
00:32:31.955 --> 00:32:36.293
No one's heard that story except
for you. because you're who you are.

509
00:32:36.376 --> 00:32:39.129
Why don't you put all that torture you
put me and Karen through to good use?

510
00:32:39.212 --> 00:32:40.923
Now would be the time.

511
00:32:41.006 --> 00:32:42.340
Counsel. we about ready?

512
00:32:42.424 --> 00:32:44.051
Uh. one more moment. Your Honor.

513
00:32:45.093 --> 00:32:47.721
Did you read the notes
from Schoonover and Lee?

514
00:32:47.805 --> 00:32:48.806
Yeah.

515
00:32:48.889 --> 00:32:50.223
Okay. here's the play.

516
00:32:50.307 --> 00:32:51.558
Walk Frank through his story.

517
00:32:51.642 --> 00:32:54.269
Connect the dots between the
Colonel and the neurologist.

518
00:32:54.352 --> 00:32:56.939
We don't have to prove that
Frank's version of events is true.

519
00:32:57.022 --> 00:32:59.482
We just have to convince
the jury that he believes it.

520
00:32:59.566 --> 00:33:00.859
and he relives it every day.

521
00:33:00.943 --> 00:33:03.445
We can put this guy in the
loony bin. where he belongs.

522
00:33:03.528 --> 00:33:04.947
- Counsel?
-  Yeah.

523
00:33:05.030 --> 00:33:08.200
Uh. Your Honor. the Defense would
like to call Frank Castle to the stand.

524
00:33:08.283 --> 00:33:11.036
Bailiff. bring in the defendant. please.

525
00:33:18.585 --> 00:33:20.713
Tell me what's going on.

526
00:33:20.796 --> 00:33:23.465
Frank's wearing a suit.

527
00:33:23.548 --> 00:33:26.677
He looks better than I ever
have. and he's not even wearing a tie.

528
00:33:33.391 --> 00:33:36.061
Order.

529
00:33:42.400 --> 00:33:44.527
Think
about what you want. Frank.

530
00:33:51.659 --> 00:33:54.204
- Something's not right.
- No turning back now.

531
00:33:55.330 --> 00:33:57.833
Do you solemnly
swear that you will tell the truth.

532
00:33:57.916 --> 00:33:59.418
the whole truth. and
nothing but the truth.

533
00:33:59.501 --> 00:34:00.960
so help you God?

534
00:34:01.920 --> 00:34:03.046
Yeah.

535
00:34:05.132 --> 00:34:07.175
Please state
your name for the record.

536
00:34:07.259 --> 00:34:08.718
Frank Castle.

537
00:34:21.940 --> 00:34:25.527
Mr. Castle. you've been
charged with multiple capital crimes.

538
00:34:25.610 --> 00:34:29.990
Been called a killer
incapable of empathy or remorse.

539
00:34:30.073 --> 00:34:31.616
Hmm.

540
00:34:31.699 --> 00:34:33.285
Yeah.

541
00:34:33.368 --> 00:34:34.452
So I hear.

542
00:34:35.495 --> 00:34:36.496
Frank...

543
00:34:36.579 --> 00:34:38.206
May I call you Frank?

544
00:34:42.878 --> 00:34:44.046
Yeah.

545
00:34:44.129 --> 00:34:47.632
Frank. we've heard a lot
about neuro-chemistry...

546
00:34:47.715 --> 00:34:49.843
and psychology. and
all things unfolding.

547
00:34:49.927 --> 00:34:52.429
scientifically and
otherwise. inside your brain.

548
00:34:53.764 --> 00:34:55.891
But I just have one
question I want to ask.

549
00:34:58.060 --> 00:34:59.895
What happened that day?

550
00:34:59.978 --> 00:35:02.730
The day your family was
so tragically killed.

551
00:35:12.282 --> 00:35:13.784
It's okay. Frank.

552
00:35:14.409 --> 00:35:16.744
- I understand. it's difficult.
-  Do you?

553
00:35:18.705 --> 00:35:19.915
Do you understand?

554
00:35:21.666 --> 00:35:24.211
'Cause I don't think
you understand shit.

555
00:35:32.385 --> 00:35:35.013
I'd like permission to treat the
witness as hostile. Your Honor?

556
00:35:35.097 --> 00:35:36.139
Granted.

557
00:35:36.223 --> 00:35:38.266
All right. Frank.

558
00:35:38.350 --> 00:35:41.103
You don't want to
tell us? I'll tell you.

559
00:35:41.186 --> 00:35:43.646
I'm gonna tell you
exactly what kind of man you are.

560
00:35:45.232 --> 00:35:47.192
You're the kind of man this city needs.

561
00:35:47.860 --> 00:35:50.904
Because. ladies and gentlemen of the
jury. we all know this city needs help.

562
00:35:50.988 --> 00:35:52.530
Needs it now.

563
00:35:52.614 --> 00:35:54.950
Not tomorrow. not next
week. not when the day comes.

564
00:35:55.033 --> 00:35:58.245
when the corruption that Wilson Fisk left
in his wake is flushed out for good.

565
00:35:58.328 --> 00:36:00.622
and the police force is
finally back on its feet.

566
00:36:00.705 --> 00:36:02.374
We need it now.

567
00:36:03.166 --> 00:36:04.877
'Cause this city's been sick.

568
00:36:05.878 --> 00:36:08.171
And the cops. they can't
fix it alone. they need...

569
00:36:08.255 --> 00:36:12.259
We all need men and women who are willing
to take the fight themselves.

570
00:36:12.342 --> 00:36:14.427
The kind of people who risk their lives

571
00:36:14.511 --> 00:36:17.014
so that we can walk safe at
night in our own neighborhoods.

572
00:36:17.097 --> 00:36:20.767
The ones our esteemed District
Attorney here is trying so hard to destroy.

573
00:36:20.851 --> 00:36:22.936
New York needs these people.

574
00:36:23.020 --> 00:36:25.856
We need... heroes.

575
00:36:27.357 --> 00:36:28.717
Order.

576
00:36:30.443 --> 00:36:32.737
The help they offer...

577
00:36:33.655 --> 00:36:35.532
and the hope that they provide.

578
00:36:37.325 --> 00:36:41.079
Frank Castle wanted to
help. but he took it too far.

579
00:36:41.163 --> 00:36:43.331
He shot people. he killed people.

580
00:36:43.415 --> 00:36:44.707
It's against the law.

581
00:36:44.791 --> 00:36:47.794
And he broke that law many. many times.

582
00:36:47.878 --> 00:36:49.754
Now. I don't like
him any more than you do.

583
00:36:49.837 --> 00:36:52.049
but here's the thing. he's
not a common criminal.

584
00:36:52.132 --> 00:36:54.217
He's not malicious in intent.

585
00:36:54.301 --> 00:36:56.803
Frank Castle is actually
a good man. He just...

586
00:36:56.887 --> 00:36:59.367
He doesn't know the difference
between right and wrong anymore.

587
00:36:59.389 --> 00:37:01.183
And he doesn't need punishment for that.

588
00:37:01.266 --> 00:37:02.434
He needs help.

589
00:37:02.517 --> 00:37:03.810
Our help.

590
00:37:06.813 --> 00:37:09.066
That's the kind of man Frank Castle is.

591
00:37:11.234 --> 00:37:14.279
And now. you have to decide what
kind of jury you want to be.

592
00:37:16.698 --> 00:37:18.366
No further questions. Your Honor.

593
00:37:20.327 --> 00:37:21.453
Your. uh...

594
00:37:22.412 --> 00:37:23.538
Your Honor?

595
00:37:24.539 --> 00:37:25.958
Can I say something?

596
00:37:26.959 --> 00:37:28.376
You may.

597
00:37:28.460 --> 00:37:30.253
You know those. uh...

598
00:37:31.546 --> 00:37:33.548
Those people?

599
00:37:34.632 --> 00:37:37.260
The ones I put down.
the people I killed?

600
00:37:38.720 --> 00:37:40.555
I want you to know that
I'd do it all again.

601
00:37:40.638 --> 00:37:42.958
This is a circus. all right?

602
00:37:42.975 --> 00:37:44.810
It's a charade. it's an act.

603
00:37:44.845 --> 00:37:46.478
- It's bullshit about how crazy I am.
- Language.

604
00:37:46.561 --> 00:37:48.230
I ain't crazy!

605
00:37:48.313 --> 00:37:49.857
I'm not crazy.

606
00:37:49.940 --> 00:37:50.941
Okay?

607
00:37:51.942 --> 00:37:53.610
I know what I did.

608
00:37:55.237 --> 00:37:57.322
I know who I am.

609
00:37:57.405 --> 00:37:59.532
And I do not need your help.

610
00:38:02.285 --> 00:38:05.998
I'm smack-dab in the middle
of my right goddamn mind.

611
00:38:06.081 --> 00:38:07.665
and any scumbag. any...

612
00:38:07.749 --> 00:38:11.919
any lowlife. any maggot piece of
shit that I put down. I did it...

613
00:38:12.004 --> 00:38:13.713
- because I liked it!
- Order!

614
00:38:13.796 --> 00:38:16.841
Hell. I loved it! I'm sittin'
here. I'm... I'm just itching.

615
00:38:16.924 --> 00:38:19.302
I'm itching to do it again.

616
00:38:19.386 --> 00:38:22.597
And you think... What. you think
you're gonna send me to a nuthouse?

617
00:38:22.680 --> 00:38:25.642
Some doctor. they're gonna get me
to stop from doing what I want to do?

618
00:38:25.725 --> 00:38:27.978
Well. that ain't
happening! Not on my watch!

619
00:38:29.062 --> 00:38:31.356
You people. you call me the
Punisher. ain't that right?

620
00:38:31.439 --> 00:38:32.607
The big bad Punisher.

621
00:38:32.690 --> 00:38:34.090
- Bailiff.
- Well. here I am!

622
00:38:34.109 --> 00:38:35.778
- Remove the witness.
-  You want it. you got it!

623
00:38:35.860 --> 00:38:38.195
I am the Punisher! I'm right here!

624
00:38:38.280 --> 00:38:40.198
You want it. I'll give it to you.

625
00:38:40.282 --> 00:38:42.379
And
anybody who came here today

626
00:38:42.404 --> 00:38:44.101
to hear me whine. to hear me beg?

627
00:38:44.161 --> 00:38:46.204
Well. you can kiss my ass!

628
00:38:46.913 --> 00:38:48.665
Do you hear me? I'm guilty.

629
00:38:48.748 --> 00:38:51.418
Come on. please. Judge!
I'm guilty. you hear me?

630
00:38:51.501 --> 00:38:53.503
I'm guilty! I'm guilty!

631
00:38:53.586 --> 00:38:56.548
I'll kill every one of
'em! I'll kill every single one!

632
00:38:58.675 --> 00:38:59.926
How the hell did this happen?

633
00:39:00.010 --> 00:39:01.303
That wasn't the
Frank I met with yesterday.

634
00:39:01.386 --> 00:39:02.762
Guys...

635
00:39:02.845 --> 00:39:05.557
- I think somebody got to him.
- Convincing him of what?

636
00:39:05.640 --> 00:39:07.892
Yelling his way to
multiple life sentences?

637
00:39:07.975 --> 00:39:09.936
- You provoked him.
-  What? I didn't...

638
00:39:09.977 --> 00:39:11.978
- What are you talking...
- I had it lined up for you.

639
00:39:12.022 --> 00:39:13.023
We could have done this.

640
00:39:13.106 --> 00:39:14.941
We could have gotten
the charges reduced.

641
00:39:15.025 --> 00:39:17.277
All you had to do was get
Frank to tell his story.

642
00:39:17.360 --> 00:39:18.996
Instead you veer off
into vigilante-land!

643
00:39:19.021 --> 00:39:20.345
Foggy. he wasn't cooperating!

644
00:39:20.738 --> 00:39:21.739
I'm glad we lost.

645
00:39:21.823 --> 00:39:23.450
You hear me? I'm glad.

646
00:39:23.533 --> 00:39:24.992
- Foggy...
- Karen. let him go.

647
00:39:25.077 --> 00:39:26.078
I don't want to hear it.

648
00:39:26.161 --> 00:39:27.495
Karen. can I talk to you
for five seconds. please?

649
00:39:27.579 --> 00:39:29.664
I don't want to hear another
bullshit excuse!

650
00:39:30.540 --> 00:39:33.335
Maybe you are an
alcoholic. Maybe you're in a fight club.

651
00:39:33.418 --> 00:39:35.712
Maybe you are sleeping with
a whole harem of women.

652
00:39:35.795 --> 00:39:37.213
I don't care. I'm done.

653
00:39:40.007 --> 00:39:41.884
You're right.

654
00:39:41.968 --> 00:39:44.220
This city really needs heroes.

655
00:39:46.264 --> 00:39:47.474
But you're not one of them.

656
00:39:57.900 --> 00:39:59.902
You gotta feel like shit.

657
00:40:01.279 --> 00:40:02.530
Go back to bed.

658
00:40:04.991 --> 00:40:06.993
I can barely stand.

659
00:40:08.035 --> 00:40:10.205
Then go back to bed.

660
00:40:15.668 --> 00:40:17.712
No.

661
00:40:21.966 --> 00:40:24.511
I don't want to be with you anymore.

662
00:40:25.970 --> 00:40:27.472
I want to be with him.

663
00:40:28.014 --> 00:40:30.558
- Don't be stupid.
- He needs more training.

664
00:40:30.642 --> 00:40:32.059
The Hand is new to him...

665
00:40:32.144 --> 00:40:33.895
Soft.

666
00:40:33.978 --> 00:40:35.897
Matt Murdock is soft.

667
00:40:35.980 --> 00:40:37.482
He made you soft.

668
00:40:37.565 --> 00:40:40.402
You let your guard down.

669
00:40:40.485 --> 00:40:43.155
Go back to bed. Ellie.

670
00:40:43.238 --> 00:40:45.865
- I'm not a child.
- You can't be with him.

671
00:40:45.948 --> 00:40:47.033
Why?

672
00:40:49.869 --> 00:40:51.413
You can't change what you are.

673
00:40:51.496 --> 00:40:54.081
Matthew thinks I can.

674
00:40:54.166 --> 00:40:56.626
And I believe him.

675
00:41:01.631 --> 00:41:02.965
Get out...

676
00:41:04.259 --> 00:41:05.635
before I get nasty.

677
00:41:05.718 --> 00:41:07.429
Are you threatening me?

678
00:41:07.512 --> 00:41:09.597
You're damn right. I am.

679
00:41:13.810 --> 00:41:14.977
Go.

680
00:41:21.234 --> 00:41:23.486
What do you think he'll say...

681
00:41:25.029 --> 00:41:27.073
when he finds out...

682
00:41:27.157 --> 00:41:28.575
what you are?

683
00:41:30.243 --> 00:41:31.869
What you've always been?

684
00:41:33.413 --> 00:41:36.123
Haven't told him yet...

685
00:41:36.208 --> 00:41:37.834
have ya?

686
00:41:40.753 --> 00:41:42.672
Get out.

687
00:41:42.755 --> 00:41:45.383
Aside from saving your ass...

688
00:41:47.677 --> 00:41:52.682
you have no idea what
I've protected you from.

689
00:41:52.765 --> 00:41:54.559
I can protect myself.

690
00:42:00.565 --> 00:42:02.108
We'll find out.

691
00:42:20.543 --> 00:42:24.714
Enough with these amateurs. Time
to get the band back together.

692
00:42:24.797 --> 00:42:26.258
Head to the Wall.

693
00:43:44.669 --> 00:43:45.962
Where's Stick?

694
00:43:48.715 --> 00:43:50.425
I made my choice.

695
00:43:51.718 --> 00:43:53.428
He didn't like it.

696
00:43:56.723 --> 00:43:58.933
I want to be with you.

697
00:44:00.352 --> 00:44:04.105
The only person in this
world who believes I'm good.

698
00:44:24.250 --> 00:44:26.293
You lost today.

699
00:44:28.045 --> 00:44:29.714
It doesn't matter.

700
00:44:32.967 --> 00:44:34.844
You lost more than just the case.

701
00:44:38.931 --> 00:44:39.932
Yeah.

702
00:44:40.016 --> 00:44:41.601
I didn't lose you.

703
00:44:47.899 --> 00:44:49.233
I'm sorry.

704
00:44:50.943 --> 00:44:52.194
I'm not.

705
00:45:02.121 --> 00:45:03.831
How does this work?

706
00:45:05.583 --> 00:45:06.876
You and me?

707
00:45:10.254 --> 00:45:12.089
How can we make it work?

708
00:45:13.090 --> 00:45:14.592
I don't know.

709
00:45:16.385 --> 00:45:18.763
But we're gonna figure it out.

710
00:45:22.349 --> 00:45:24.101
Not now. though.

711
00:45:28.731 --> 00:45:30.858
Right now. you need to rest.

712
00:48:03.761 --> 00:48:07.431
Who do you work for? Huh?

713
00:48:07.514 --> 00:48:09.642
Who sent you?

714
00:48:09.726 --> 00:48:11.894
Answer me! Huh?

715
00:48:13.437 --> 00:48:15.439
You tell
them. whoever they are.

716
00:48:15.522 --> 00:48:19.360
I'm gonna find them. and when
I do. I'm gonna...

717
00:48:24.531 --> 00:48:26.242
No...

718
00:48:26.325 --> 00:48:28.995
You're... You're just a kid.

719
00:48:31.205 --> 00:48:33.582
Elektra. no... No...

720
00:48:52.894 --> 00:48:54.270
What did you do?

721
00:49:08.660 --> 00:49:10.703
This is who I am.

722
00:49:16.500 --> 00:49:18.502
Do you still want me?

723
00:49:24.175 --> 00:49:25.176
Matthew.

724
00:49:25.259 --> 00:49:27.511
Matthew!

725
00:49:31.974 --> 00:49:34.143
You're okay... You're okay...

726
00:49:46.405 --> 00:49:47.907
I got this one.

727
00:49:47.990 --> 00:49:49.200
On whose orders?

728
00:49:49.283 --> 00:49:51.994
The warden's. You got
a problem with that?

729
00:49:52.078 --> 00:49:54.205
No one tells us anything down here.

730
00:50:15.852 --> 00:50:18.771
Hey. look at
me. Frank! Look at me!

731
00:50:18.855 --> 00:50:20.272
I'm gonna stick you!

732
00:50:20.356 --> 00:50:22.649
That's a promise!

733
00:50:22.734 --> 00:50:24.401
I promise you!

734
00:51:51.280 --> 00:51:52.406
Right through here.

735
00:52:42.581 --> 00:52:44.583
I see you got my message.

736
00:52:45.305 --> 00:53:45.501
